From 2422f4238818988e11274608bf2636b75191f987 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: Exynos9820 syscore suspend/resume handling

The generic syscore save/restore of the CMU register caches does not
fit a SoC sleep on Exynos 9820:

 - a CMU whose power domain is off is not saved or restored,
 - CMUs owned by the APM firmware (CMU_MIF0..3), the CPU clusters
   (CMU_CPUCL0/2) and the always-on CMU_TOP, CMU_CORE and CMU_BUSC are
   not written back,
 - only registers that changed are rewritten,
 - CMU_TOP is compared with its suspend state after the sleep: the
   changed leaf muxes, dividers and gates of blocks that are powered
   off at that point are rewritten, and every difference is logged
   after the resume.

A resume hook, called before each register cache is restored, lets the
suspend code leave a breadcrumb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
