+/*
+ * Resume class of each CMU_TOP register (SAMSUNG_RESUME_*, see
+ * samsung_clk_aon_resume() in clk.c). CMU_TOP is always on and shared with the APM and the CP;
+ * its cache is not written back at syscore resume. Only the leaf
+ * mux/div/gate of blocks that are off (LEAF) or quiescent (IO) while the
+ * syscore resume runs may be rewritten. Never: PLLs, MUX_PLL_SHARED and the
+ * PLL_SHARED dividers, CMU_BOOST, CPUCL0/1/2 and MIF switches, CPUCL0_DBG,
+ * APM/BUSC/CORE/MIF_BUSP/PERIS bus, FSYS0/FSYS0A/FSYS1/PERIC0/PERIC1 bus (INT
+ * DVFS members), DPU/DPU_BUS (DISP DVFS, display running), G3D_SWITCH (the
+ * APM's PLL_G3D relock fallback), HPM, CMUREF, BUS_OTF, MODEM_SHARED0/1.
+ */
